```c
qsort(entries, entry_count, sizeof(char *), 
      (int (*)(const void *, const void *))strcmp);
```

The issue is that `strcmp` expects `const char *`, but we're casting to compare `char **`. The comparison function for qsort receives pointers to the array elements, so it gets `char **` and needs to dereference.

